From 0e9d91cc2d0e969de2b39de6c17185e84fe8dd14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:59:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(site): a build that fell back to npm install says so
 in the run summary

site.yml ran `npm ci || npm install`: when package-lock.json no longer matched
package.json, npm ci failed and the deploy went on with npm install, which resolves
versions afresh, and nothing in the run said the deployed bundle was not the
locked one. The fallback stays, so a drifted lockfile cannot stall the hourly
content deploy, but it now prints a workflow warning naming the cause.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit a0fb8790f07b60ea6a298392e671891259dbfbdd)
---
 .github/workflows/site.yml | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/site.yml b/.github/workflows/site.yml
index d00b978..eb3a905 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/site.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/site.yml
@@ -104,7 +104,10 @@ jobs:
         with:
           node-version: 22
       - name: Install
-        run: npm ci || npm install
+        # the fallback keeps the hourly deploy going when package-lock.json has drifted from
+        # package.json, but that build resolves versions afresh; it is announced in the run
+        # summary rather than passing in silence
+        run: npm ci || { echo "::warning title=package-lock.json out of sync::npm ci failed; built with npm install instead — regenerate the lockfile"; npm install --no-audit --no-fund; }
       - name: Build
         run: npm run build
       - name: Generate language landing pages, library pages and sitemap
